      "text": "Pandemics emerge when a virus from an animal reservoir acquires the ability to\nspread efficiently in a naive human population. The mathematical epidemiology\nframework — built on the basic reproduction number R₀ — predicts transmission\ndynamics, herd immunity thresholds, and intervention effects."
    },
    {
      "id": "08-PANDEMIC-BIOLOGY.md#003",
      "path": [
        "08-PANDEMIC-BIOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:virology:08-pandemic-biology, git-history:virology:08-pandemic-biology]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/08-PANDEMIC-BIOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[pandemic, biology]",
        "current_path": "virology/08-PANDEMIC-BIOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:virology:pandemic-biology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "virology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
